\n1. Microservices - Definition, architecture patterns, challenges, when to use\n2. Service Boundaries - Defining boundaries, bounded contexts, design techniques\n3. Domain-Driven Design - DDD principles, ubiquitous language, aggregates\n4. CAP Theorem - Consistency, availability, partition tolerance trade-offs\n5. Service Communication - Synchronous vs asynchronous patterns\n6. Advanced Communication - Event-driven, sagas, choreography\n7. Backend for Frontend - BFF pattern, aggregation, transformation\n8. Service Discovery - Registries, health checks, load balancing\n9. Circuit Breaker - Cascading failure prevention, resilience\n\nEach concept page has 2000-2500 words of university-level content with real-world examples, code samples, diagrams, and key takeaways. Links are displayed as a beautiful 3-column grid with gradient backgrounds and hover effects.","tree":{"sha":"bfc50e19b95f22b233d895c41643219834b0ecc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/trees/bfc50e19b95f22b233d895c41643219834b0ecc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/commits/187804386b1a2b6098ca75118142977ebbb39480","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/187804386b1a2b6098ca75118142977ebbb39480","node_id":"C_kwDOQKXz-doAKDE4NzgwNDM4NmIxYTJiNjA5OGNhNzUxMTgxNDI5NzdlYmJiMzk0ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9","sha":"21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9"}],"sha":"187804386b1a2b6098ca75118142977ebbb39480","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/187804386b1a2b6098ca75118142977ebbb39480"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-27T23:09:20Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-27T23:09:20Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"message":"Checkpoint: Added 10 comprehensive concept pages (20,000+ words) to Module 1:\n1. Microservices - Definition, architecture, challenges, when to use\n2. Service Boundaries - Defining boundaries, bounded contexts, design techniques\n3. Domain-Driven Design - Ubiquitous language, aggregates, value objects, entities\n4. CAP Theorem - Consistency, availability, partition tolerance, trade-offs\n5. Service Communication - Synchronous (REST, gRPC) vs Asynchronous (message queues)\n6. Advanced Communication - Event-driven, sagas, choreography vs orchestration\n7. Backend for Frontend - BFF pattern, aggregation, transformation\n8. Service Discovery - Registries, health checks, load balancing\n9. Circuit Breaker - Preventing cascading failures, resilience patterns\n\nEach page includes:\n- University-level technical depth\n- Real-world examples and case studies\n- Practical code examples\n- Visual diagrams and tables\n- Key takeaways\n- Navigation between concepts\n\nUpdated App.tsx routing to include all concept pages. Ready for production use as a comprehensive CS learning resource.","tree":{"sha":"f6e9d3bf08dbc5135fb152d621e7ae841a180ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/trees/f6e9d3bf08dbc5135fb152d621e7ae841a180ea5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/commits/21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/21ee60f304c3d2968e028eb49a2f89228dbd12e9","node_id":"C_kwDOQKXz-doAKDIxZWU2MGYzMD