es\n✓ Real-world debugging case study: slow checkout diagnosis\n✓ SLO/SLI definitions with e-commerce examples\n✓ Error budgets: 99.95% uptime = 21.6 minutes monthly budget\n✓ Performance budgets: enforcing bundle size limits per team\n✓ Incident response playbook: detection → triage → mitigation → RCA\n✓ Post-mortem template for learning from failures\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALITY:\n✓ University-level technical explanations suitable for CS students\n✓ Real metrics from major companies (Spotify, Uber, Airbnb, Netflix)\n✓ Practical code examples for every concept\n✓ Performance analysis with actual numbers and percentages\n✓ Trade-offs and architectural decisions explained\n✓ Debugging techniques and troubleshooting guides\n✓ Complete course covering 25+ advanced concepts\n\nALL 5 MODULES NOW COMPLETE AT UNIVERSITY LEVEL:\nModule 1: Microservices & BFF (E-commerce case study)\nModule 2: SSR/Hydration (Netflix selective hydration)\nModule 3: Core Web Vitals & SEO (Airbnb optimization)\nModule 4: Code-Splitting & Module Federation (Spotify & Uber)\nModule 5: Team Structure & Observability (Conway''s Law & SLOs)","tree":{"sha":"cc6e7e7706fd9fb0ef691a1f7b384c8ee6986ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/trees/cc6e7e7706fd9fb0ef691a1f7b384c8ee6986ffc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/commits/03a5a237493249df9a132cba710a96a7671f1fa7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/03a5a237493249df9a132cba710a96a7671f1fa7","node_id":"C_kwDOQKXz-doAKDAzYTVhMjM3NDkzMjQ5ZGY5YTEzMmNiYTcxMGE5NmE3NjcxZjFmYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87","sha":"9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87"}],"sha":"03a5a237493249df9a132cba710a96a7671f1fa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/03a5a237493249df9a132cba710a96a7671f1fa7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:48:09Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:48:09Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"message":"Checkpoint: Modules 2 and 3 Enhanced to University Level:\n\nMODULE 2 - The Frontend Fragmentation (SSR/Hydration):\n✓ React Fiber Architecture & Reconciliation algorithm explained\n✓ Advanced SSR concepts with CSR vs SSR comparison\n✓ Hydration process deep dive with real blocking time analysis\n✓ Real-world Netflix case study: Selective hydration reducing hydration time from 2000ms to 200ms\n✓ Progressive Hydration pattern with React.lazy and Suspense examples\n✓ Islands Architecture as alternative approach (Astro example)\n✓ Hydration mismatch debugging techniques with Chrome DevTools\n✓ Time-dependent rendering pitfalls with code examples\n✓ Practical troubleshooting guides for production issues\n\nMODULE 3 - Measuring Success (Web Performance & SEO):\n✓ Core Web Vitals deep dive: LCP, FID/INP, CLS with thresholds\n✓ LCP optimization strategies: Critical rendering path, lazy loading, SSR, CDN\n✓ FID/INP blocking time analysis with real Netflix example\n✓ Long task breaking patterns with code examples\n✓ Web Workers for off-main-thread computation\n✓ CLS prevention strategies: Image dimensions, ad space reservation, font-display swap\n✓ Real-world Airbnb case study: 57% LCP improvement, 70% FID improvement, 72% CLS improvement\n✓ Technical SEO: CSR vs SSR for search engines\n✓ Structured Data (JSON-LD) with product example\n✓ Web Vitals API implementation with monitoring code\n✓ Performance profiling tools: Chrome DevTools, React Profiler, Lighthouse, WebPageTest\n\nEDUCATIONAL QUALITY:\n✓ University-level technical explanations suitable for CS students\n✓ Real metrics from major companies (Netflix, Airbnb, Amazon)\n✓ Practical code examples for every concept\n✓ Performance analysis with actual numbers\n✓ Trade-offs and architectural decisions explained\n✓ Debugging techniques and troubleshooting guides","tree":{"sha":"c9e77507fd50479002920337cbf843e76bbf6dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/trees/c9e77507fd50479002920337cbf843e76bbf6dc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/commits/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87","node_id":"C_kwDOQKXz-doAKDlhNWU5NmVmMTViMGYxY2Y0MTJjMjk4MjNiY2QyYzNjYmMwMDFkODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6","sha":"ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6"}],"sha":"9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/9a5e96ef15b0f1cf412c29823bcd2c3cbc001d87"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:40:59Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:40:59Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"message":"Checkpoint: Module 1 Enhanced with University-Level Technical Depth:\n\nTECHNICAL ADDITIONS:\n✓ Domain-Driven Design (DDD) and Bounded Contexts\n✓ CAP Theorem (Consistency, Availability, Partition Tolerance)\n✓ Advanced communication patterns:\n  - Circuit Breaker pattern for failure handling\n  - Service Discovery (Consul, Kubernetes DNS)\n  - API Gateway pattern\n✓ Service communication deep dive (sync vs async with detailed trade-offs)\n\nREAL-WORLD CASE STUDY - E-Commerce Product Page:\n✓ Complete Amazon-style product page request flow\n✓ Actual JSON payload examples for each microservice\n✓ Step-by-step breakdown of BFF aggregation process\n✓ Performance analysis: Sequential (380ms) vs Parallel (150ms) requests\n✓ Real latency numbers from each service\n\nTECHNICAL EXAMPLES:\n✓ JWT token validation\n✓ Promise.all() parallel request pattern\n✓ Service response transformation\n✓ Data aggregation logic\n\nEDUCATIONAL VALUE:\n✓ University-level explanations of distributed systems concepts\n✓ Real performance metrics and optimization strategies\n✓ Practical code examples showing BFF implementation\n✓ Trade-off analysis for architectural decisions\n\nModule 1 now provides complete technical understanding suitable for advanced computer science students and experienced engineers.","tree":{"sha":"6a603740868e3f8416d168e5ca6c7d758fd34f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/trees/6a603740868e3f8416d168e5ca6c7d758fd34f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/git/commits/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6","node_id":"C_kwDOQKXz-doAKGFkOWU5NDkxZmViNzgyMmEyYzE0NjhkY2Q4MDdmYTY3YTRkNzdkZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commit/16bfbdaa980c5e34bf47ee8889821393334b5c0d","sha":"16bfbdaa980c5e34bf47ee8889821393334b5c0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/16bfbdaa980c5e34bf47ee8889821393334b5c0d"}],"sha":"ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/ad9e9491feb7822a2c1468dcd807fa67a4d77dd6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/architecture-course/commits/16bfbdaa980c5e34bf47ee8889821393334b5c0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:35:42Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-27T22:35:42Z","email":"sandbox@manus.ai","name":"Manus Sandbox"},"message":"Checkpoint: Comprehensive content improvements completed:\n\nHIGH PRIORITY IMPROVEMENTS:\n✓ Module 1: Added Microservices Challenges, Service Communication Patterns, When NOT to use Microservices\n✓ Module 2: Added Hydration Pitfalls, Progressive Hydration, Islands Architecture sections\n✓ Module 3: Added Tools & Measurement (Lighthouse, Web Vitals API), Optimization Strategies, CLS Prevention examples\n✓ Module 4: Added Rollback Strategies, Error Handling, Shared State Management, Performance Budgets\n✓ Module 5: Added Monitoring & Observability (Logs, Metrics, Traces), SLOs, Incident Response, Team Communication & Governance\n\nMEDIUM PRIORITY IMPROVEMENTS:\n✓ Added real-world case studies and examples throughout\n✓ Added Common Pitfalls sections (Hydration Mismatches, CLS Issues, Version Management)\n✓ Added practical troubleshooting guides\n✓ Added version management and breaking changes policies\n✓ Added rollback strategies and incident response procedures\n\nAll modules now include:\n- Deep explanations following Tony Alicea''s teaching style\n- Interactive visualizations and diagrams\n- Practical code examples\n- Real-world challenges and solutions\n- Clear key takeaways\n- Trade-offs and \"weird parts\" highlighted throughout","tree":{"sha":"d8477c129c5d0c46ba3eb4c6645b12c74a4a9683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franruedaesq/a