com/users/dkdoc7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkdoc7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/archi-duke/RAGaaS/commits/d6956f0422020ee3eb3bc1e5991379e769228fa0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T22:26:27Z","email":"duke.kimm7@gmail.com","name":"duke.kimm"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T22:26:27Z","email":"duke.kimm7@gmail.com","name":"duke.kimm"},"message":"fix(frontend): rebase standalone entry on /ragaas/ build base\n\nApply the 2026-07-07 platform notice: standalone entry via the gateway\n(/ragaas/) rendered a blank page because built index.html referenced\nassets at root-absolute paths (/env.js, /assets/...), which the gateway\nlongest-prefix routing sent to the shell.\n\n- vite.config: base ''/ragaas/'' at build time only (dev serve and shell\n  remote loading are unaffected — remoteEntry resolves chunks relative\n  to its own load URL)\n- App.tsx: BrowserRouter basename from BASE_URL, applied only when the\n  URL actually carries the /ragaas prefix (direct :80 access and dev\n  keep no basename)\n- config.ts: rebase API fallbacks on BASE_URL — in shell mode\n  window._env_ is the shell''s env.js (no REACT_APP_RAGAAS_API), so the\n  fallback is the live path; it must target {origin}/ragaas/api/v2 to\n  traverse the gateway\n- nginx.conf: strip /ragaas prefix for direct (non-gateway) access so\n  the rebased absolute references keep working on host port 80\n- docs: import ragaas-notice-2026-07-07.md (shell tab enabled, fix\n  instructions, answers on tarball/WS auth/Kendo license/dev port)\n\nVerified through the gateway: index refs all /ragaas/-prefixed, env.js\nand bootstrap chunk 200 application/javascript, deep-link refresh 200,\nremoteEntry/api regression 200; direct :80 access also 200 via rewrite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AMnZ6fuSmxfNNTtKsspHLM","tree":{"sha":"470c4022fb8a